1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,080
Meditation.

2
00:00:02,280 --> 00:00:07,320
You want to try it, but when you actually do, it doesn't really work, does it?

3
00:00:07,870 --> 00:00:12,478
You close your eyes and sit, and somehow there are even more thoughts.

4
00:00:12,678 --> 00:00:17,898
Tomorrow's to-do list, something someone said, an old memory out of nowhere.

5
00:00:18,098 --> 00:00:22,526
And eventually you give up, thinking, maybe meditation just isn't for me.

6
00:00:23,076 --> 00:00:26,064
If you're new to meditation, that's completely normal.

7
00:00:26,264 --> 00:00:28,028
It's not that you're bad at it.

8
00:00:28,227 --> 00:00:30,424
You just did things in the wrong order.

9
00:00:30,624 --> 00:00:37,356
Sitting still and stopping your thoughts from the very start is hard even for people who've practiced for years.

10
00:00:37,906 --> 00:00:40,461
So at first, don't sit.

11
00:00:40,662 --> 00:00:42,318
Move first.

12
00:00:42,868 --> 00:00:44,524
But it's not just about moving.

13
00:00:44,724 --> 00:00:48,072
It's about the few seconds right after you stop moving.

14
00:00:48,272 --> 00:00:49,460
A tiny gap.

15
00:00:49,660 --> 00:00:53,656
How you use that gap is what today is really about.

16
00:00:54,206 --> 00:00:56,294
Awakening doesn't come through the head.

17
00:00:56,494 --> 00:00:57,897
It comes through the body.

18
00:00:58,098 --> 00:01:05,190
Today, I'll talk about how to use your body to quiet your thoughts, and how to plant what you want in the gap when they stop.

19
00:01:05,390 --> 00:01:08,810
And at the end, we'll get up and do it together.

20
00:01:09,960 --> 00:01:13,199
Thoughts are always off in the past or the future.

21
00:01:13,399 --> 00:01:15,812
But your body is always here, now.

22
00:01:16,362 --> 00:01:18,342
And emotions stay in the body.

23
00:01:18,542 --> 00:01:29,378
Psychiatrist Bessel van der Kolk, in his book The Body Keeps the Score, describes how wounds that words couldn't reach often begin to loosen only when the body starts to move.

24
00:01:29,928 --> 00:01:35,148
That's why heavy energy only clings tighter when you try to think it away.

25
00:01:35,348 --> 00:01:37,832
You have to shake it out, through the body.

26
00:01:38,382 --> 00:01:42,774
On Earth, your body is your soul's instrument, and its antenna.

27
00:01:42,974 --> 00:01:46,286
When the instrument is stiff, it's hard to hear your soul.

28
00:01:47,436 --> 00:01:52,008
That's why, for thousands of years, people met God through dance.

29
00:01:52,558 --> 00:01:58,246
Sufis dress in white and spin, one palm turned to the sky, one to the earth.

30
00:01:58,446 --> 00:02:04,530
They turn, and turn, until the self disappears, and it's said they become one with God.

31
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:09,723
Korean shamans opened the door to other worlds with drums and dance.

32
00:02:09,924 --> 00:02:15,000
And Native Americans cleansed body and mind with sweat, in the heat of the sweat lodge.

33
00:02:15,550 --> 00:02:17,926
Science says something similar.

34
00:02:18,126 --> 00:02:24,318
When you move enough to sweat, your body releases chemicals that lift your mood.

35
00:02:24,518 --> 00:02:32,654
And in an Oxford University study, when people danced together in sync, their tolerance for pain went up, and they felt much closer to each other.

36
00:02:33,204 --> 00:02:37,308
When we move together, we go beyond me, and remember us.

37
00:02:38,458 --> 00:02:40,762
And all of these have one thing in common.

38
00:02:40,962 --> 00:02:42,185
They stop thought.

39
00:02:42,736 --> 00:02:51,736
Milton Erickson, often called the father of modern hypnotherapy, would deliberately keep talking in confusing, monotonous ways.

40
00:02:51,935 --> 00:02:58,343
As the conscious mind tried to follow and wore itself out, at some point thinking would let go.

41
00:02:58,543 --> 00:03:02,215
And in that gap, people slipped into deep trance.

42
00:03:02,766 --> 00:03:04,962
Zen koans work the same way.

43
00:03:05,161 --> 00:03:06,170
What is this?

44
00:03:06,369 --> 00:03:13,965
You hold on to a question the mind can never solve, again and again, until thinking reaches a dead end, and simply snaps.

45
00:03:14,165 --> 00:03:17,693
That moment becomes the door to awakening.

46
00:03:18,243 --> 00:03:20,223
The body works the same way.

47
00:03:20,423 --> 00:03:27,299
Dance until you're out of breath, move until the sweat runs, and for just a moment, thinking stops completely.

48
00:03:27,849 --> 00:03:29,577
Thought is like a gatekeeper.

49
00:03:29,777 --> 00:03:33,521
When it's awake, it blocks the way: that'll never work.

50
00:03:33,721 --> 00:03:39,265
But in the moment the gatekeeper dozes off, that's your chance to let what you want slip through.

51
00:03:40,415 --> 00:03:42,971
So why do we meditate, really?

52
00:03:43,521 --> 00:03:47,733
For most people, it's because they want to be happy while they're here in this world.

53
00:03:47,933 --> 00:03:50,885
Healthy, abundant, at peace.

54
00:03:51,435 --> 00:03:58,743
Of course, some people meditate because they want to expand their consciousness so far that they won't need to come back to Earth.

55
00:03:58,943 --> 00:04:00,779
That's a beautiful path too.

56
00:04:01,329 --> 00:04:05,757
But today, I'll talk about the kind of meditation most people want.

57
00:04:05,957 --> 00:04:09,953
Meditation for living better, here, in this world.

58
00:04:10,153 --> 00:04:14,689
Quieting the mind, and in that stillness, picturing the life you want.

59
00:04:15,239 --> 00:04:19,380
In that gap, picture what you want as one vivid scene.

60
00:04:19,930 --> 00:04:24,106
Not a goal, not a sentence, but like a scene from a movie.

61
00:04:24,306 --> 00:04:29,202
Where you are, who you're with, what you see, what you hear.

62
00:04:29,752 --> 00:04:32,164
And load that scene with big emotion.

63
00:04:32,364 --> 00:04:38,376
Overflowing joy, gratitude, happiness so strong it brings tears.

64
00:04:38,926 --> 00:04:42,526
In an earlier video, I said to imagine joyfully.

65
00:04:42,726 --> 00:04:46,470
This gap is when that imagining sinks in the deepest.

66
00:04:46,670 --> 00:04:50,990
While the gatekeeper rests, that scene goes in, unblocked.

67
00:04:51,540 --> 00:04:55,860
And of course, you can also just rest in that stillness without picturing anything at all.

68
00:04:56,060 --> 00:05:01,100
The longer you stay there, the more you feel connected to something deeper in the universe.

69
00:05:01,300 --> 00:05:03,028
That's a wonderful time too.

70
00:05:04,178 --> 00:05:09,758
If you're new to meditation, try just these three things, starting today.

71
00:05:09,958 --> 00:05:13,846
Sitting meditation can wait until this feels familiar.

72
00:05:14,396 --> 00:05:16,700
One, one song a day.

73
00:05:16,900 --> 00:05:20,212
When no one's watching, dance however you want.

74
00:05:20,412 --> 00:05:22,500
You don't have to be good at it.

75
00:05:23,050 --> 00:05:31,690
Two, right after you finish dancing or exercising, while you're still out of breath, close your eyes and picture one scene you want.

76
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:38,468
Three, on heavy days, before you start thinking, shake out your whole body for three minutes.

77
00:05:39,018 --> 00:05:42,906
Go at your own pace, within what your body can handle.

78
00:05:43,106 --> 00:05:45,374
Even gentle shaking is enough.

79
00:05:46,524 --> 00:05:48,648
So let's do it together, right now.

80
00:05:48,848 --> 00:05:51,044
If you can, stand up.

81
00:05:54,594 --> 00:05:57,222
First, shake out your hands.

82
00:05:57,422 --> 00:05:59,330
Loosely, easily.

83
00:06:09,880 --> 00:06:11,356
Now your shoulders too.

84
00:06:11,556 --> 00:06:14,364
As if you're shaking off everything you carried today.

85
00:06:24,914 --> 00:06:26,678
Now your whole body.

86
00:06:26,878 --> 00:06:30,334
Knees, feet, shake however you like.

87
00:06:30,534 --> 00:06:33,342
Feel the heavy energy draining down into the floor.

88
00:06:53,892 --> 00:06:55,548
Now, stop.

89
00:06:55,748 --> 00:07:00,284
Stand still, close your eyes, and just feel your breath.

90
00:07:08,834 --> 00:07:11,390
Notice how quiet your thoughts are right now.

91
00:07:14,940 --> 00:07:17,964
In this gap, picture one scene you want.

92
00:07:23,514 --> 00:07:26,394
In that scene, what's the look on your face?

93
00:07:31,944 --> 00:07:33,060
Who's there with you?

94
00:07:38,610 --> 00:07:41,022
What feeling is rising in your chest?

95
00:07:49,572 --> 00:07:52,128
Hold that feeling, take a deep breath in…

96
00:07:56,328 --> 00:07:59,964
and as you slowly breathe out, open your eyes.

97
00:08:04,114 --> 00:08:08,002
If meditation has felt hard, don't start by sitting.

98
00:08:08,202 --> 00:08:09,498
Start by moving.

99
00:08:09,698 --> 00:08:13,010
Awakening isn't something you understand with your head.

100
00:08:13,210 --> 00:08:15,874
It's something you remember with your body.

101
00:08:16,424 --> 00:08:22,760
Shake it out through the body, and in the gap when thought stops, plant the scene you want, with big emotion.

102
00:08:23,310 --> 00:08:26,406
And when we move together, we remember.

103
00:08:26,606 --> 00:08:27,902
I'm not alone.

104
00:08:28,102 --> 00:08:29,290
We are us.

105
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:32,612
Today, dance to just one song.

106
00:08:32,812 --> 00:08:36,700
And tell me in the comments which song it was.

107
00:08:37,250 --> 00:08:38,438
Play your own game.
